    what: "M2 (#39, #43): a Tool Station left loaded -- three parts staged and the assembled pickaxe still sitting in the output slot -- saved when the container was four slots wide. #152 grew it to six for the Tool Forge's large tools (three inputs became five, and the output moved from index 3 to index 5), and this is what proves that growth is additive rather than a save break: all four stacks come back, in order, and the nested pickaxe's pre-#196 `tool_materials` gets its `parts` list rebuilt on the way (the migration reaches items inside a container, not just items in a hand). Two things worth knowing about the shape: SimpleContainer's list is positionless -- entries are written in slot order and read back with `addItem`, so an empty slot compacts rather than being preserved -- and because of that the pickaxe reloads into index 3, which is now an input slot rather than the output. It is handed back to the player by ToolStationMenu#returnUnusableInputs on the first tab that does not use that slot; visible relocation, no loss. Also the only fixture carrying a part item's `forgeweave:material` component and a station's crafted-from `texture`."
